{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1140960-rules-for-glamour-type","id":1140960,"title":"Rules for Glamour type?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-16T20:07:25-07:00","id":1140960,"title":"Rules for Glamour type?","content":"I seem to remember that in &quot;Keys to the Kingdom&quot; there was supposed to be some rule on the different types of Glamour. Given how certain Chimera are literally the stuff of Nightmares, has C20 indicated a rule for using Glamour and Dross from things of Nightmare and how it can affect Changelings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T23:36:43-07:00","id":1140995,"title":"","content":"There were rumours that such rules would have been introduced in the now lost Book of Glamour, but unfortunately C20 offers us no answers recarding dark Glamour. <br /> <br /> Personally I tried adressin it in my contribution to the open call way back but the word count was strict and it seems my writing was not impressive enough.<br /> <br /> Perhaps future supplements will delve deeper into the differences between Glamour and dark Glamour and even give us better, non banal, ways to harvest the sweet essence of Nightmares.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T03:53:56-07:00","id":1141014,"title":"","content":"Ah yes, Book of Glamour is what I was thinking about. What was Keys to the Kingdom? A second book that didn't make it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T05:03:18-07:00","id":1141023,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Book of Glamour was going to update Changeling's magic system to revised standards without actually being a revised edition, kind of like how the Players Guide overhauled first edition's magic system.<br /> <br /> Keys to the Kingdom was going to Changeling's Year of the Scarab tie in. It was going to explore the Middle East from a changeling perspective and also be a major chronicle book in which the players retrieve the Triumph Casque of Sorrows. The opening fiction for it can be found at <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0BymGBI7sN3MsNTJkNzhjN2YtZTcxMy00Y2VkLWFjYzktMDA2ZDk1ZDY4M2M4\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/open?id=0By...A2ZDk1ZDY4M2M4</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T06:57:50-07:00","id":1141052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1140960-rules-for-glamour-type?p=1140995#post1140995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There were rumours that such rules would have been introduced in the now lost Book of Glamour, but unfortunately C20 offers us no answers recarding dark Glamour.<br /> <br /> Personally I tried adressin it in my contribution to the open call way back but the word count was strict and it seems my writing was not impressive enough.<br /> <br /> Perhaps future supplements will delve deeper into the differences between Glamour and dark Glamour and even give us better, non banal, ways to harvest the sweet essence of Nightmares.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Since I wrote the Dark Glamour section (first draft because we never got to second before the cancellation) for the Book of Glamour, I can tell you that the version from back then won't make any sense now since it was to fuel fear, destruction and outright horrors. All of those &quot;flavors&quot; are now clearly baked into what Glamour is in C20. In C20 Glamour is Glamour regardless of &quot;flavor&quot;. I don't know if Dark Glamour turns into a special subject somewhere along the road, but the old - Book of Glamour - version would not work in C20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Krister M. Michl</b> <hr /><b>Freelance writer</b> <hr /><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Krister_M._Michl\" target=\"_blank\">Entry on White Wolf Wikipedia</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2494-rigistrade","name":"Rigistrade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2494_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T07:22:12-07:00","id":1141059,"title":"","content":"I always thought, that Dark Glamour was not a metaphysical distinction, but categorical, opinion-based. Like, there's acts and there's &quot;evil&quot; acts.<br /> <br /> From the physics standpoint both are things, that happen. Nothing more, nothing less.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T08:44:41-07:00","id":1141077,"title":"","content":"So basically Glamour is now Glamour and dark Glamour as a concept doesnt really exist anymore, meaning the answer to OP's question is that there are no special effects for Changeling using Glamour taken from Nightmare beings unless the ST deems so. <br /> <br /> The problem still remains though that even C20 unfortunately forgot to give any rules to use Reverie to inspire fear and terror, as all the musing tresholds are still about positive emotions. Currently the rules can be used to inspire a mortals creativity so that the mortal then spreads terror to his fellow men in inspired ways but there is no way to directly inspire terror to gain Glamour apart from Ravaging but that requires one to use Banality to steal Glamour. There should be a non banal way for the Nightmare Kithain and especially Thallain to harvest Glamour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T08:51:36-07:00","id":1141080,"title":"","content":"You can inspire positive feelings about sadistic and cruel acts to others...<br /> <br /> Like really creative maniac.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T09:52:31-07:00","id":1141097,"title":"","content":"So my personal thought on the matter is that the stuff that tended to be labeled as dark glamour in 2nd edition is just glamour - positive and negative emotions both encompass the human condition, so either can be mused equally.<br /> <br /> In my mind, dark glamour is what results when people retreat from higher order thoughts and emotions, instead embracing primal drives and instincts.<br /> <br /> Of course, the dividing line between the two isn't terribly clear. Humans are just another kind of animal, after all, but it's that which is uniquely human that separates Tuatha from Fomorian and, likewise, Kithain from Thallain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T10:57:06-07:00","id":1141128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1140960-rules-for-glamour-type?p=1141097#post1141097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So my personal thought on the matter is that the stuff that tended to be labeled as dark glamour in 2nd edition is just glamour - positive and negative emotions both encompass the human condition, so either can be mused equally.<br /> <br /> In my mind, dark glamour is what results when people retreat from higher order thoughts and emotions, instead embracing primal drives and instincts.<br /> <br /> Of course, the dividing line between the two isn't terribly clear. Humans are just another kind of animal, after all, but it's that which is uniquely human that separates Tuatha from Fomorian and, likewise, Kithain from Thallain.</div> </div> </div> </div>But what would you say about Musing Tresholds?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T11:59:04-07:00","id":1141152,"title":"","content":"I'd rather save my thoughts on musing thresholds for now. I'd like to work on future Changeling books. If I get a chance to expand on musing thresholds, the book might require something different than what I'd do right at this moment \ud83d\ude09","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T12:03:21-07:00","id":1141154,"title":"","content":"Am I the only one who thinks it would be VERY Banal, to say, that Glamour gained through Ravaging, cant be used to heal, or inspire. or such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T12:07:21-07:00","id":1141157,"title":"","content":"Oh sure, glamour gained through ravaging is glamour. It can be used in all the ways changelings use glamour. It's just a mildly banal way to acquire it. New glamour isn't generated; existing glamour is ripped from a person. Overall, gathering glamour through ravaging diminishes the total glamour in the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T12:11:36-07:00","id":1141159,"title":"","content":"Assuming glamour is generated by dreamers, and not taken by dreamers from the Dreaming <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T19:37:54-07:00","id":1142000,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping to see more details on Glamour in upcoming C20 supplements. Having more information and clarification on this topic would be really helpful, and should generate new story ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://imgbb.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://image.ibb.co/fzeOgQ/1172c70f3ff188688852c74c8145285c_original_2_4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> Visit my freehold for Changeling links, settings, art, and other goodies.<br /> <a href=\"https://theshepherdsfreehold.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The Shepherd's Freehold</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13648-shepherd","name":"Shepherd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T00:09:32-07:00","id":1142058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1140960-rules-for-glamour-type?p=1141159#post1141159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming glamour is generated by dreamers, and not taken by dreamers from the Dreaming <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>In Denizens of The Dreaming, the denizens... of the Dreaming known as norns believed, that the source of all Glamour is somewhere in Autumn World. And, you know, they live... in the Dreaming, so gotta be experts on what is or isn't in the Dreaming. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}